<!--# 🧩 Adding Poppins Font to Android (Jetpack Compose)-->

<!--This project uses **Poppins** as the primary font family.-->
<!--Follow the steps below to set it up correctly for Jetpack Compose typography.-->

<!-- -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--## 📁 Font Files-->

<!--We’re using two weights from the Poppins family:-->

<!-- - **`poppins_regular.ttf`** → Normal weight (for general text)-->
<!-- - **`poppins_medium.ttf`** → Medium weight (for headers, buttons, etc.)-->

<!--These are both `.ttf` (TrueType Font) files — think of them like `.png` files but for text.-->
<!--They define how your letters look inside the app.-->

<!-- -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--## 🗂️ Where to Get the Fonts-->

<!--Download them directly from **[Google Fonts → Poppins](https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Poppins)**-->

<!--1. Click **“Download family”**-->
<!--2. Extract the `.zip` file-->
<!--3. Inside, locate these files:-->
<!--```-->

<!--Poppins-Regular.ttf-->
<!--Poppins-Medium.ttf-->

<!--```-->
<!--4. (Optional) Rename them for consistency:-->
<!--```-->

<!--poppins_regular.ttf-->
<!--poppins_medium.ttf-->

<!--```-->

<!-- -&#45;&#45;-->

<!--## 📦 Where to Put Them-->

<!--Create a folder under your `res` directory called **`font`** (if it doesn’t exist):-->

<!--```-->

<!--app/-->
<!--└─ src/-->
<!--└─ main/-->
<!--└─ res/-->
<!--└─ font/-->
<!--├─ poppins_regular.ttf-->
<!--└─ poppins_medium.ttf-->

<!--````-->

<!--Android Studio will automatically detect them as font resources (if not, rebuild once).-->

<!-- -&#45;&#45;-->

